  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Kirchoff&#39;s Equation-<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#916;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#916;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><munderover><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>298</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></munderover><msub><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#916;</mo><mi>Cp</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>reac</mi></msub><mi>dT</mi></math><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#916;</mo> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>reac</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> is dependent on temperature.<br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>K</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>CO</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>&#215;</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>&nbsp; as solids are treated at unit activity. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is independent of initial amount of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>pCO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;at a given temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></math> depends only on temperature.<br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mtext>H</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <msub> <mtext>E</mtext> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>for</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </msub> <mo>-</mo> <msub> <mtext>E</mtext> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>back</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </msub> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;</p><p>A catalyst lowers only the activation energies &amp; <math> <mrow> <mo>&#916;</mo> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>react</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> is independent of catalyst.</p>",
